# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — repository-root build-context exclusions.
#
# Both container images build from the REPOSITORY ROOT: docker/docker-compose.yml
# sets `context: ..` for the `api` and `frontend` services, and both Dockerfiles
# carry `# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1` (BuildKit). BuildKit resolves the ignore
# file as `<context>/.dockerignore`, so this single repo-root file governs the
# build context sent to the daemon for BOTH docker/api.Dockerfile and
# docker/frontend.Dockerfile.
#
# Why this file exists (production-readiness hardening — see MIGRATION_NOTES.md §7.2):
#   1. HERMETIC, REPRODUCIBLE BUILDS regardless of host workspace state. Each
#      Dockerfile does a broad source copy AFTER its dependency-restore layer
#      (frontend.Dockerfile L19 `COPY frontend/ ./` after `npm ci`;
#      api.Dockerfile L20 `COPY backend/ backend/` after `dotnet restore`). With
#      no ignore file, a host `frontend/node_modules` (built for the host's
#      native arch, e.g. Windows/macOS) overlays the Linux `npm ci` output and
#      `npm run build` then runs wrong-architecture esbuild/rollup binaries — the
#      frontend image build fails in any "build locally, then containerize" tree.
#      Likewise a host `backend/**/obj|bin` would clobber the in-container
#      `dotnet restore`. Excluding those host artifacts makes the build depend
#      ONLY on source, so it behaves identically on a clean clone and a dirty tree.
#   2. MINIMAL CONTEXT TRANSFER. A dirty tree is otherwise ~3.45 GB (dominated by
#      frontend/.angular + frontend/node_modules and backend bin/obj) shipped to
#      the daemon for EACH image build; with this file the context is a few MB.
#   3. NO SECRETS in any build context or image layer (mirrors docker/.gitignore).
#
# NOTHING the Dockerfiles consume is excluded here:
#   api:      backend/Directory.Build.props, backend/src/**/*.csproj, all backend/
#             source, backend/src/DnnMigration.Api/appsettings*.json.
#   frontend: frontend/package*.json, frontend/src/**, frontend/angular.json,
#             frontend/tsconfig*.json, plus docker/nginx.conf (stage 2).
# This file only filters the host->daemon context; it does NOT affect files
# regenerated by RUN steps inside the build, nor `COPY --from=build` stage copies
# (so the frontend `COPY --from=build /app/dist/dnn-migration/browser` is unaffected
# by the `**/dist` rule below — that path is produced inside the build stage).
# =============================================================================

# ---- Node / Angular build artifacts (host-arch; regenerated by `npm ci`) ----
# `**/node_modules` is the critical correctness fix: it stops a host-native
# node_modules from overlaying the container's Linux `npm ci` output.
**/node_modules
**/.angular
**/dist
**/out-tsc
**/.npm
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# ---- .NET build artifacts (regenerated by `dotnet restore` / `dotnet publish`)
# Keeps host obj/bin from clobbering the in-container restore, and trims context.
**/bin
**/obj
**/out
**/artifacts
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# ---- Version control --------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
**/.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ---- Legacy DNN reference source — read-only, NOT a container build input ----
# The legacy VB.NET trees are retained as reference only and emit no target
# artifacts (AAP §0.2 / MIGRATION_NOTES §1); the new images build solely from
# backend/ and frontend/, so these are excluded from the build context.
Library/
Website/
docs/
DotNetNuke.sln
DotNetNuke_VS2008.sln
mkdocs.yml
catalog-info.yaml

# ---- Blitzy tooling / QA evidence (never part of a deployable image) --------
blitzy/

# ---- Secrets — keep them out of every build context/layer (CWE-798) ---------
# Mirrors docker/.gitignore. The non-secret template is deliberately retained.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# ---- Editor / OS / local cruft ----------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.log
**/*.binlog
**/TestResults/
**/coverage/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
